Longer method but with Graphic User Interface use Adobe Media Encoder

![image.png](spotify%20clouded/image%201.png)

i use the mpeg4 preset and export audio only, with aac vbr, 44.1 kHz, stereo, high quality, 256 kbps. the issue is that the files come out as .mp4. you’ll need to change the extension to .m4a, which you can do with PowerRename or any batch renaming tool. the drawback of using a gui is that it adds extra steps if you have to rename every file from .mp4 to .m4a, which i don’t recommend.

![image.png](spotify%20clouded/image%202.png)

*In media encoder you will notice .aac audio (mpeg-2). But it is outdated, less efficient at the same bitrate, and less compatible across platforms and cannot retain artwork images or rich metadata compared to .m4a (aac in mpeg-4).*

on pc or mac, enable *local files* in spotify settings and add the folder where your music is stored. spotify will automatically detect all subfolders.

![image.png](spotify%20clouded/image%203.png)

i recommend adding your music to a drive: once uploaded, you can simply download it on any device and spotify will read it. formats like flac or wav are not supported, so stick to m4a.

